maluos-agents (0.3.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Phase 13 slice 2, delegation (docs/phase13-slice2-delegation.md): the
    list shows the estate's directory with each agent's node, capability
    tags and accept policy; an answer carries its provenance (the agent,
    its node, the model calls, the envelope); the Policy page is real for
    a local agent (accept_from, the classification ceiling, approve — saved
    through pkexec maluctl agent policy) and shows the directory's policy
    for an estate agent; "Make my personal agent" (maluctl agent create me
    --personal) with its weekly renewal; the Inbox page (the person's
    estate inbox: decisions, replies, read); --self-test reports the
    directory count, the personal agent and the inbox.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:00:00 +0000

maluos-agents (0.2.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Self-test: the UI-ready deadline is 240 s, not 90 s. A cold first
    launch of the WebKitGTK window on a slow machine (the boot test under
    TCG, with every library read from disk) overran 90 s while the same
    launch a minute later, warm, passed; the deadline only guards the
    self-test against a page that never reports ready.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 23:45:00 +0000

maluos-agents (0.2.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Phase 12 slice 9: Talk draws the answer as it grows (tasks/send
    without waiting, tasks/get once a second while the task works); the
    office's page for an agent loads with the desk's identity (the desk
    token as the Bearer header on its first request, so the office can
    answer with a session cookie); the Control and Activity pages re-read
    every 30 s while visible, the logs every 5 s while the unit is active.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 01:06:51 +0000

maluos-agents (0.1.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * First version (Phase 12 slice 8, the Agents app): maluos-agents, a
    WebKitGTK window over the session's state listing the local agents and
    the office's, with Talk (the task interface of maluos_agent_tasks,
    local socket or the office's task URL), Control (AgentAction, logs,
    a one-off command), Policy (delegations and grants from the vault,
    the office's card), Memory (the agent's compartment) and Activity (the
    vault's ledger, the office's activity endpoint); the office's own page
    for an agent loads beside it. `maluos-agents --sync` writes the icons:
    launchers, the Agents app folder in the grid, ~/Desktop/Agents.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
